	abstract = {Alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) is a key biomarker for hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC), but 30–40\% of cases are AFP-negative. Prothrombin induced by vitamin K absence II (PIVKA-II) is more sensitive for HCC detection, though its role in systemic therapy remains underexplored. This study aimed to evaluate PIVKA-II in non-AFP-secreting HCC treated with systemic therapy.},
